#+title: Org2 Chess PGN plugin

This self-contained example plugin renders =pgn= and =chess-pgn= source blocks
as an interactive board through the shared Org2 HTML runtime. It therefore
works in =org2 export html= and OpenOrg without a separate Mac extension. It
uses the v1 process protocol and ships without an install step or third-party
dependencies.

From a corpus, install the package from this repository and explicitly trust
its resolved content hash:

#+begin_src sh
org2 plugin add https://github.com/aviaviavi/org2.git \
  --subdir examples/plugins/chess-pgn --trust --apply
#+end_src

The first install is pinned in =org2.plugins.lock.json=. Later
=org2 plugin sync --apply= reproduces that exact version; use
=org2 plugin update org2.chess-pgn --apply= to advance it deliberately.
